Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:43:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(tableaux): retain bounded diagnostics and unknown
 JSON outcomes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Explain/check JSON can report an empty trace for a refuted class, and the
explanation wrapper can turn an exhausted search into a satisfiable answer.
Retain label, unfolding, conjunction and failed-branch/clash diagnostics,
resolve concept IDs to names, and cap reported steps and step text.

Use the traced three-way verdict in the two JSON wrappers. An exhausted
search returns null plus complete=false and reason=budget_exhausted rather
than a definitive true/false. Apply the configured phase deadline when
collecting explanatory subsumption traces.

Add regressions for forced exhaustion, failed disjunction branch retention,
and diagnostic truncation. These are operational diagnostics, not a minimal
axiom proof or a complete independently checked certificate.

Extracted from local source b8cb6ce7d72a82811f3268c951857d3ccb279d1e.
Exclude adapter-owned IRI normalization and all server/storage/transport edits.
Rename the regression module and normalize branch indentation for review.

